  "body": "Objects (content-addressed; temp plus rename; a replaced file is identical). HEAD.tmp and log.tmp per process. The log appended only in the commit path, rebuilt by merge and reset (a rebuild racing an append lost lines on Unix; found on CI). The reflog append-only. The cache keyed by hash, written after HEAD advances. Claims cleaned by prune after an hour. A lock's drop removes only its own file. The event's parent is the HEAD the plan was loaded from, never HEAD re-read (the last way a writer could claim the wrong event; found on CI).",
